{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:24:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. I'm Dr. Lee, one of your hospital doctors. You came in last night with abdominal and chest pain. Can you tell me more about what happened?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:25:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes. Yesterday afternoon, my usual left upper belly pain got much worse. I took morphine, but it didn’t help much. Then I started vomiting dark green fluid—about two liters. And suddenly, I had this sharp chest pain that went from my back to the front and up to my jaw."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:26:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. The chest pain wasn’t worse with breathing or movement? And you didn’t have shortness of breath or sweating?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:27:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it wasn’t related to breathing. And I didn’t sweat or feel short of breath. But I felt hot. I’ve also been more tired than usual for weeks, and dizzy when I exercise."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:28:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Thanks. We’ve reviewed your CT scan. It shows a worsening partial small bowel obstruction due to strictures from your fibrosing mesenteritis. Your G-tube has also moved into the wrong position—past the stomach into the small bowel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:29:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh. So that’s why I’m so bloated and sick? Does that explain the chest pain too?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes. Your heart tests were normal—no heart attack. The chest pain likely came from the abdominal distension and referred pain. We’ll manage the obstruction first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. What’s the plan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep you NPO—nothing by mouth—for now. You’ll get fluids and nutrition through your IV. We’ll also replace your G-tube to make sure it’s in the stomach so we can decompress your bowel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "When will that happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Tomorrow morning. The radiology team will do it. In the meantime, we’ll control your pain and nausea with IV meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on morphine for years. Is it safe to keep using it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2183-01-06 05:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll continue it carefully. We’re also giving you pregabalin and trazodone like you take at home for nerve pain and sleep."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2183-01-07 12:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, we just finished replacing your G-tube. It’s now correctly placed in the stomach. We’ve connected it to suction to help drain fluid and reduce pressure in your bowel."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2183-01-07 12:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I already feel a little less bloated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2183-01-07 12:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a positive sign. We’ll keep monitoring your output. If it stays high, we may need to start TPN—total parenteral nutrition—through your IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2183-01-07 12:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had TPN before. It’s okay, but I’d rather eat if I can."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2183-01-07 12:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll try to get you back on food soon. But we have to be careful. Your bowel is still partially blocked."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2183-01-09 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your G-tube output is still high, so we’re starting TPN today. It will give you all the nutrition you need while your bowel rests."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2183-01-09 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Any other changes?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2183-01-09 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also adjusting your thyroid medicine. Your TSH was low, so we’re reducing levothyroxine from 100 to 75 mcg daily."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2183-01-09 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had hypothyroidism for years. That makes sense."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2183-01-11 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white blood count dropped a bit, but we think it’s from a recent infection. Everything else looks stable. No sign of infection now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2183-01-11 07:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I had bronchitis a few weeks ago. Could that be it?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2183-01-11 07:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, that’s likely. Your counts are starting to improve on their own, so we’re not worried."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2183-01-13 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to try advancing your diet to full liquids tomorrow. Your G-tube output has decreased, which is a good sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2183-01-13 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great! Can I have broth and juice?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2183-01-13 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, things like that. But we’ll watch closely. If your pain or output increases, we may need to stop and reassess."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2183-01-14 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You did well on full liquids, but your G-tube output went up again. So we’re switching you back to NPO for a few days and continuing TPN."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2183-01-14 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I was hoping to eat more. Is the blockage still there?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2183-01-14 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the obstruction is still present. We’re going to repeat the CT scan and possibly do an endoscopy to look at the blockage."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2183-01-15 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The new CT shows the same partial obstruction. The bowel beyond the blockage looks healthy, no sign of ischemia. We’ve scheduled an upper endoscopy for tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2183-01-15 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can they fix it during the scope?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2183-01-15 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly, but the blockage is high up and tight. The gastroenterologist may not be able to pass the scope through. But we’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2183-01-16 14:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The endoscopy was done. The scope couldn’t pass through the stricture. But we’re starting a new medicine—octreotide—to reduce your gastric secretions and G-tube output."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2183-01-16 14:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "How does that work?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2183-01-16 14:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a hormone injection that slows down your digestive secretions. We’ll give it three times a day. We hope it will help your bowel rest and reduce output."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2183-01-16 14:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Any side effects?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2183-01-16 14:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Some people get cramps or diarrhea, but we’ll monitor you. It’s often very helpful for patients like you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2183-01-18 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your G-tube output has decreased significantly since starting octreotide. That’s a great sign."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2183-01-18 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain is much better. I haven’t needed much morphine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2183-01-18 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Excellent. We’re going to try advancing your diet again—this time to a low-fat regular diet in small amounts."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2183-01-19 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You tolerated the low-fat diet well. We’re turning off TPN today and keeping you on oral intake. Your G-tube will stay in but we’ll reduce suction."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2183-01-19 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s a relief. What about my warfarin? I noticed it went up to 7.5 mg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2183-01-19 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, because TPN contains vitamin K, which counteracts warfarin. Now that you’re off TPN, we’re reducing it back to 5 mg daily. Your INR was 1.5 this morning—slightly low, but safe for now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2183-01-19 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my thyroid dose stayed at 75 mcg?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2183-01-19 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep it there. Your levels are now in a better range."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2183-01-21 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You had a small episode of chest pain today, similar to when you were admitted. But your EKG was normal, and the pain went away after you passed gas."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2183-01-21 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "It felt like pressure building up and then releasing. So it’s still related to the bowel?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2183-01-21 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, likely due to temporary distension. As long as it resolves quickly and your heart tests are normal, we’re not concerned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2183-01-23 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve been stable for days. Pain is at your baseline, no nausea, eating well. We’re planning for discharge in a few days."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2183-01-23 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What meds will I go home on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2183-01-23 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll continue most of your home meds. We’re adding octreotide—three times a day under the skin. And we’re keeping your levothyroxine at 75 mcg and warfarin at 5 mg."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2183-01-23 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll need a prescription for the octreotide?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2183-01-23 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll send it to your pharmacy. A nurse will teach you how to give the injections before you leave."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2183-01-24 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your follow-up is set with your gastroenterologist next week. They’ll monitor your obstruction and adjust treatment as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2183-01-24 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my INR? Should I get it checked soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2183-01-24 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your anticoagulation clinic will call you for a check within the week. Keep taking warfarin daily at the same time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2183-01-25 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing really well. We’ll discharge you tomorrow morning. You’ll go home on a low-fat diet, your regular meds, and octreotide."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2183-01-25 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. I’m glad we got the G-tube fixed and the octreotide is helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2183-01-25 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, this was a good step forward. Call us if you have increasing pain, can’t keep food down, or have a fever."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2183-01-26 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared to go home. Your condition is stable, pain is controlled, and you’re eating well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2183-01-26 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel ready. Thanks for all your help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2183-01-26 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and follow up as planned."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2183-01-06 05:24:00",
    "admission_end": "2183-01-26 16:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "The patient, a woman with fibrosing mesenteritis, recurrent small bowel obstruction, and chronic pain, was admitted for worsening abdominal pain and acute chest pain. Imaging confirmed a partial small bowel obstruction due to strictures from mesenteric fibrosis and post-pyloric migration of her G-tube. She was managed conservatively with NPO status, IV fluids, pain control, and G-tube replacement for proper decompression. TPN was initiated due to persistent high G-tube output and inability to maintain oral intake. Octreotide was started to reduce secretions, which led to decreased output and improvement in symptoms. Her chest pain, ruled out for cardiac cause, was attributed to abdominal distension. Leukopenia resolved spontaneously, and levothyroxine was adjusted for a suppressed TSH. Warfarin dosing was modified due to vitamin K in TPN. She was transitioned to a low-fat diet, discontinued TPN, and discharged home on octreotide with follow-up planned.",
    "problems": [
      "Unspecified intestinal obstruction",
      "Sclerosing mesenteritis",
      "Mechanical complication due to other implant and internal device, not elsewhere classified",
      "Chronic hepatitis C without mention of hepatic coma",
      "Sicca syndrome",
      "Mitral valve disorders",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, unspecified",
      "Disorder of bone and cartilage, unspecified",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Other chest pain",
      "Leukocytopenia, unspecified",
      "Anemia of other chronic disease",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Unspecified acquired hypothyroidism",
      "Insomnia, unspecified",
      "Depressive disorder, not elsewhere classified",
      "Personal history of venous thrombosis and embolism"
    ]
  }
}
